WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:19.428
<v Host>Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya, your host. Today is May twenty-fourth. This is our very first episode. Today's story: more foreigners are visiting Japan than ever before. The number just passed thirty million. Let's listen.

00:00:20.027 --> 00:00:27.564
<v News>去年、日本に来た外国人の数が3000万人を超えました。

00:00:28.263 --> 00:00:37.384
<v News>一番多い国は中国です。次は韓国、そしてアメリカです。

00:00:38.084 --> 00:00:45.835
<v News>外国人に人気がある場所は、東京、大阪、京都です。

00:00:46.536 --> 00:00:53.496
<v News>最近は、北海道や沖縄に行く人も増えています。

00:00:54.195 --> 00:01:01.396
<v News>外国人がたくさん来るので、ホテルの値段が高くなっています。

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:14.215
<v News>日本語が分からなくて困る外国人もいます。駅やレストランで、英語のメニューや案内が増えています。

00:01:14.915 --> 00:01:22.763
<v News>日本政府は、「もっと多くの外国人に来てほしい」と言っています。

00:01:23.463 --> 00:01:31.144
<v Host>All right. This story uses simple, everyday Japanese. Perfect for beginners. Let's break it down.

00:01:31.743 --> 00:01:33.519
<v Host>The first sentence.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:42.183
<v Slow>去年、日本に来た外国人の数が3000万人を超えました。

00:01:42.983 --> 00:01:50.280
<v Host>Last year, the number of foreigners who came to Japan exceeded thirty million. Let's look at the key words.

00:01:50.879 --> 00:01:52.896
<v Vocab>去年

00:01:53.296 --> 00:01:56.968
<v Host>Last year. One of the first time words you learn.

00:01:57.567 --> 00:02:00.183
<v Vocab>外国人

00:02:00.584 --> 00:02:07.376
<v Host>Foreigner. The three characters mean outside, country, person. Very logical.

00:02:07.975 --> 00:02:10.448
<v Vocab>超えました

00:02:10.848 --> 00:02:16.151
<v Host>Exceeded, passed. When a number goes over a target, you use this verb.

00:02:16.752 --> 00:02:18.527
<v Host>Where are the visitors from?

00:02:19.127 --> 00:02:28.895
<v Slow>一番多い国は中国です。次は韓国、そしてアメリカです。

00:02:29.695 --> 00:02:35.312
<v Host>The country with the most visitors is China. Next is South Korea, then America.

00:02:35.912 --> 00:02:38.816
<v Vocab>一番多い

00:02:39.216 --> 00:02:47.111
<v Host>The most. The first word means number one, the second means many. Together: the most numerous.

00:02:47.711 --> 00:02:49.463
<v Vocab>次

00:02:49.864 --> 00:02:54.183
<v Host>Next. Short and useful. You'll hear it everywhere.

00:02:54.783 --> 00:02:56.632
<v Host>What places are popular?

00:02:57.231 --> 00:03:05.560
<v Slow>外国人に人気がある場所は、東京、大阪、京都です。

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:11.376
<v Host>The places popular with foreigners are Tokyo, Osaka, and Kyoto.

00:03:11.975 --> 00:03:14.639
<v Vocab>人気がある

00:03:15.039 --> 00:03:23.776
<v Host>Popular. Literally, it means has people's spirit. You can use this for anything — a restaurant, a song, a person.

00:03:24.376 --> 00:03:26.463
<v Vocab>場所

00:03:26.864 --> 00:03:31.207
<v Host>Place, location. A basic but very important word.

00:03:31.807 --> 00:03:33.391
<v Host>And new trends.

00:03:33.991 --> 00:03:41.455
<v Slow>最近は、北海道や沖縄に行く人も増えています。

00:03:42.256 --> 00:03:48.063
<v Host>Recently, the number of people going to Hokkaido and Okinawa is also increasing.

00:03:48.663 --> 00:03:51.015
<v Vocab>最近

00:03:51.415 --> 00:03:56.599
<v Host>Recently. Use it at the beginning of a sentence to talk about current trends.

00:03:57.199 --> 00:03:59.864
<v Vocab>増えています

00:04:00.264 --> 00:04:07.032
<v Host>Is increasing. The ongoing form means it's a change that's still happening. Very common in news.

00:04:07.632 --> 00:04:09.240
<v Host>There's a side effect.

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:17.567
<v Slow>外国人がたくさん来るので、ホテルの値段が高くなっています。

00:04:18.367 --> 00:04:22.783
<v Host>Because many foreigners are coming, hotel prices have gone up.

00:04:23.384 --> 00:04:25.663
<v Vocab>たくさん

00:04:26.064 --> 00:04:29.975
<v Host>A lot, many. Very basic, very useful.

00:04:30.576 --> 00:04:32.663
<v Vocab>値段

00:04:33.064 --> 00:04:37.384
<v Host>Price. You can say the price is high, or the price is cheap.

00:04:37.983 --> 00:04:39.591
<v Host>And a challenge.

00:04:40.192 --> 00:04:46.072
<v Slow>日本語が分からなくて困る外国人もいます。

00:04:46.872 --> 00:04:51.096
<v Host>There are also foreigners who don't understand Japanese and have trouble.

00:04:51.696 --> 00:04:54.216
<v Vocab>分からない

00:04:54.615 --> 00:04:58.911
<v Host>Don't understand. One of the most important verbs in Japanese.

00:04:59.512 --> 00:05:01.600
<v Vocab>困る

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:08.672
<v Host>To be in trouble, to have difficulty. When you're lost in Japan and can't read the signs — that feeling.

00:05:09.271 --> 00:05:10.663
<v Host>The solution.

00:05:11.264 --> 00:05:18.512
<v Slow>駅やレストランで、英語のメニューや案内が増えています。

00:05:19.312 --> 00:05:24.543
<v Host>At stations and restaurants, English menus and guides are increasing.

00:05:25.144 --> 00:05:27.399
<v Vocab>案内

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:32.000
<v Host>Guide, information. You'll see this on signs everywhere.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:34.567
<v Host>And what the government says.

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:43.351
<v Slow>日本政府は、もっと多くの外国人に来てほしいと言っています。

00:05:44.151 --> 00:05:48.279
<v Host>The Japanese government says they want even more foreigners to come.

00:05:48.879 --> 00:05:51.016
<v Vocab>もっと

00:05:51.415 --> 00:05:56.456
<v Host>More, even more. A very handy word for everyday conversation.

00:05:57.055 --> 00:05:59.696
<v Vocab>来てほしい

00:06:00.096 --> 00:06:07.824
<v Host>Want someone to come. This pattern means you want someone else to do something. It's different from when you say what you yourself want to do.

00:06:08.423 --> 00:06:11.423
<v Host>Let's listen to the full story one more time.

00:06:12.024 --> 00:06:19.560
<v News>去年、日本に来た外国人の数が3000万人を超えました。

00:06:20.259 --> 00:06:29.379
<v News>一番多い国は中国です。次は韓国、そしてアメリカです。

00:06:30.079 --> 00:06:37.831
<v News>外国人に人気がある場所は、東京、大阪、京都です。

00:06:38.531 --> 00:06:45.492
<v News>最近は、北海道や沖縄に行く人も増えています。

00:06:46.192 --> 00:06:53.391
<v News>外国人がたくさん来るので、ホテルの値段が高くなっています。

00:06:54.091 --> 00:07:06.211
<v News>日本語が分からなくて困る外国人もいます。駅やレストランで、英語のメニューや案内が増えています。

00:07:06.911 --> 00:07:14.759
<v News>日本政府は、「もっと多くの外国人に来てほしい」と言っています。

00:07:15.459 --> 00:07:18.196
<v Host>Quiz time. Three questions.

00:07:18.795 --> 00:07:24.915
<v Slow>去年、何人の外国人が日本に来ましたか？

00:07:25.716 --> 00:07:30.444
<v Host>How many foreigners came to Japan last year? Over thirty million.

00:07:31.043 --> 00:07:35.315
<v Slow>一番多い国はどこですか？

00:07:36.115 --> 00:07:39.572
<v Host>Which country has the most visitors? China.

00:07:40.172 --> 00:07:44.732
<v Slow>ホテルの値段はどうなっていますか？

00:07:45.531 --> 00:07:49.012
<v Host>What's happening to hotel prices? They're going up.

00:07:49.612 --> 00:08:02.788
<v Host>That's the first episode of Japanese Daily News. Full transcript with furigana at podcast.jpnotes.dev. Subscribe on Apple Podcasts or Spotify. See you tomorrow.

00:08:03.387 --> 00:08:05.788
<v News>また明日。
